This would allow you to still use the old very simple resugar_str function and have the readback of substrings in a malformed string like mentioned in this todo.

Another alternative would be to first resugar all constructors ignoring the existence of lists and strings, and then right after try to construct the list and string sugars from the constructors. That would also make the code a bit cleaner i think
```
// in resugar_adts
match term {
  ...
  Term::Lam {tag, ...} => {
    if book.adt.contains(tag) {
      // Tries to recover this constructor and calls resugar_adt recursively
      *term = rebuild_constructors(body);
      match tag {
        // Since this function is recursive, if the constructor fields were lists or strings, they will already have been resugared, making these 2 resugar_functions simpler.
        Tag::string => resugar_string(term)
        Tag::list => resugar_list(term)
      }
    }
  }
  ...
}
```

